{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790258237,"nonce":"4wWZCe737t5PI6YkZV/NUJbxx+s=","title":"Inliner: cold error paths and allocations make a small callee call-bearing","message":"`classify()` set has_calls for every direct call and for `Intrinsic::Malloc`/`Free`, and counted the whole body against MAX_INLINE_INSTS_WITH_CALLS (48). So a leaf constructor (malloc plus stores) was call-bearing and never inlined outside a loop, and a callee whose only calls sit on error arms (Lua's zl_index_nil/zl_annotate arms, Python's zb_fatal arms, a method with a raise path) was refused as too large although its hot path is tiny. `loops_or_dispatches()` counted a malloc as a call toward the dispatch limit, and `classify_recursive()` counted cold calls the same way.\n\nFix: one notion of a real call (`is_real_call`: not a cold callee, not a box reader, not Malloc/Free) used by classify, loops_or_dispatches and classify_recursive; has_calls and the call-bearing size cap count only the blocks that can reach the return without a cold call (`blocks_leading_to_cold` complement). The 64/256 caps and MAX_POST_INLINE_INSTS still count the whole body.","files":null}]}